\section{Discussion}

In this work, we presented a non-convolutional detection system that operates on native point cloud data. The goal of the proposed method is to better match the sparsity of point cloud data, and also allow the system to be flexibly targeted across a range of computational priorities. We demonstrate that the resulting detector is competitive with state-of-the-art detection systems on the KITTI object detection benchmark \cite{geiger2013vision}, and can outperform a competitive convolutional baseline on the large-scale \datasetname.

